#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:5
#: 5fbbfabcb349474893e6114196278c0e
msgid "Initial Tuning Flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:8
#: a662dc7a87af4382b55d617ca5080c4b
msgid "Pilot's preparation for first flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:10
#: cdab392e68404145bf9959828bbc9b18
msgid "The first takeoff of an untuned multirotor is the most dangerous seconds of the aircraft’s life. This is where the aircraft could be very unstable causing a sudden increase in power when then results in the aircraft jumping into the air, or it may be so poorly tuned that you have insufficient control over the aircraft once it is airborne. The pilot should be extremely diligent during the tuning flights to avoid a situation that could result in injury or damage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:12
#: a1b84cd549314dc6afebaab0a494dde3
msgid "There are several things that the pilot can do to minimise the risk during the early tuning process:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:14
#: e454e879efda41cd8932a3443161326f
msgid "The pilot should conduct a motor number and orientation check (see :ref:`Checking the motor numbering with the Mission Planner Motor test <connect-escs-and-motors_testing_motor_spin_directions>`). Care should be taken to ensure that the correct frame type is selected. Incorrect frame type can result in a very fast yaw rotation or complete loss of control. Take note of the output percentage required to spin the propellers and ensure that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:16
#: bbd7969641294293913e3ec30e494f81
msgid ":ref:`MOT_SPIN_ARM <MOT_SPIN_ARM>` is set high enough to spin the motors cleanly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:17
#: 71987d75790a4017ba337818c2aee63a
msgid ":ref:`MOT_SPIN_MIN <MOT_SPIN_MIN>` is set high enough to spin the motors with a minimal level of thrust."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:19
#: 437716eaeac1483ca39169e8fb4cb742
msgid "All flights after a significant tuning change should be done in Stabilize. Stabilize provides the pilot with significantly more control over the aircraft in the event that the attitude controllers are unstable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:20
#: c8a878d52e894297b2a5f172099805ed
msgid "The pilot should not take off in AltHold until the altitude controller has been tested in flight. This should be done by taking off in Stabilize and switching to Alt Hold. While Alt Hold is rarely a problem unless the aircraft has a very low hover throttle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:21
#: 225a0f3598b347cb85b3bfb08f303889
msgid "For the initial flights the pilot should ensure that these parameters are set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:23
#: 389802bb85a6490ca64c3815a8a264af
msgid ":ref:`ATC_THR_MIX_MAN <ATC_THR_MIX_MAN>` to 0.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:24
#: fee0f9ea4cf34cdd8f8b9da865ef3b8f
msgid ":ref:`MOT_THST_HOVER <MOT_THST_HOVER>` to 0.25 (or lower than the expected hover throttle)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:26
#: 8fa6232f5d0e4d878341b5055267da78
msgid "Use a radio and calibrate the radio correctly (see :ref:`common-radio-control-calibration`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:27
#: f3c3afaa77a4450f8924a043d6b82a10
msgid "Configure an Emergency Stop Motors switch and test it (see :ref:`Auxiliary Functions <common-auxiliary-functions>`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:28
#: d16cf504a6f24d1ca57614bb4b8c72ba
msgid "Do tuning flights in low-wind condition and normal weather (no rain and between 15°C/59°F and 25°C/77°F)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:29
#: 21640652e674483d8dec401c5b7227d1
msgid "Practice STABILIZE flight in simulator or on a low-end drone first, you should be confident to be able to takeoff and land with your untuned aircraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:33
#: c7a7d10e72a243c3ad1d16aa5d59044e
msgid "First Flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:35
#: e6c5aedb6287463f99128f8b95198c31
msgid "The first take off is the most dangerous time for any multirotor. Care must be taken to ensure the aircraft is not destroyed in the first seconds of flight and nobody is injured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:37
#: 45064cdda9a440038538411e6c91971f
msgid "**Ensure that all spectators are at a safe distance**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:38
#: 513d225c4699489b998d1c988db601c1
msgid "**Ensure the pilot is at a safe distance and position**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:39
#: f2edd81bed114eed9e5299a5bacee3f1
msgid "The pilot should refresh themselves on the method used to disarm the aircraft (using :ref:`Auxiliary Functions <common-auxiliary-functions>` for Motor Interlock or Arm/Disarm may be beneficial)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:41
#: 7686f7a2aaa440f6a089287e3f2062c1
msgid "This flight will allow to setup your aircraft in a \"flyable for tuning\" state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:43
#: c039b16c610a4bf6a344fe42496cb1d0
msgid "Ensure the aircraft is in STABILIZE mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:44
#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:46
#: b2ae1636cac243ffa6a7ccb50f317697
#: 4762fa47d7284f60a20fb019c1ad12a8
msgid "Arm the aircraft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:45
#: 3885cef6867947c3bf0b496ecfe9ef09
msgid "Immediately disarm the aircraft to ensure your disarm procedure is correct"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:47
#: c6bc18c7627844daa5144772e401f316
msgid "Slowly increase the throttle looking for signs of oscillation. (long or flexible landing gear may cause some landing gear oscillation that will only go away after the aircraft leaves the ground)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:48
#: f7afeca9494546d98e5fb47915b822ce
msgid "As soon as the aircraft lifts off the ground immediately put the aircraft back down as gently as possible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:49
#: a0a4d55ae094452689591736368f80c5
msgid "Disarm the aircraft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:50
#: cbdc23a3c4df4a0199b1d0f9a02836ff
msgid "Evaluate what you observed to decide if you need to make adjustments to the tuning parameters or if it is safe to take off again"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:51
#: 602404e5c8864555b6ccace01315aabe
msgid "Arm and increase the throttle to initiate a takeoff"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:52
#: 59002bd67ff34a55a5a5cc9828759eb3
msgid "Hover at approximately 1m altitude and apply small (5 degrees) control inputs into roll and pitch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:53
#: 59c70de420394610ad84f85d1dd2eb5b
msgid "Immediately land if any oscillation is observed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:55
#: c901b7dfd46a406da8ecaaa358f099ac
msgid "Next section will explain how to remove the oscillations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:58
#: 3d22950abc6c4c2fa0d07351cb0aa172
msgid "Initial aircraft tune"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:60
#: 807101db0ded4a5b833ab441fd7dfed2
msgid "The first priority when tuning an multirotor aircraft is to establish a stable tune, free of oscillations, that can be used to do further tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:62
#: 7611193debb047b298235c828871e9d6
msgid "Arm the aircraft in STABILIZE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:63
#: 5ff365f79ab74f559244220fe40db01d
msgid "Increase the throttle slowly until the aircraft leaves the ground"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:64
#: 358b2b6650ce439ca880682264f72105
msgid "If the aircraft starts to oscillate immediately abort the takeoff and/or land the aircraft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:65
#: 9c9088a396484d27a218e8c54c6b563a
msgid "Reduce all the following parameters by 50%"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:67
#: 2584f53cceec4c1084dc25af58cddac9
msgid ":ref:`ATC_RAT_PIT_P <ATC_RAT_PIT_P__AC_AttitudeControl_Multi>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:68
#: 98575bac059d4a7b903e2193b090be7d
msgid ":ref:`ATC_RAT_PIT_I <ATC_RAT_PIT_I__AC_AttitudeControl_Multi>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:69
#: 4e5183a0ddc54e89b016deecb5d2b8af
msgid ":ref:`ATC_RAT_PIT_D <ATC_RAT_PIT_D__AC_AttitudeControl_Multi>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:70
#: 2f23968e0ce74c26b84bb05349411245
msgid ":ref:`ATC_RAT_RLL_P <ATC_RAT_RLL_P__AC_AttitudeControl_Multi>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:71
#: dde5887781e649b6be5d888cf7dec267
msgid ":ref:`ATC_RAT_RLL_I <ATC_RAT_RLL_I__AC_AttitudeControl_Multi>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:72
#: 5462f8edd041409ea2a24529b6410081
msgid ":ref:`ATC_RAT_RLL_D <ATC_RAT_RLL_D__AC_AttitudeControl_Multi>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:74
#: 76064030264b48c5a6923fe77f09ff14
msgid "This process is repeated until the aircraft can hover without oscillations being detectable visually or audibly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:76
#: 5d3db7446b0a4465a81b0fd163db1e84
msgid "If the aircraft has very long or flexible landing gear then you may need to leave the ground before ground resonance stops."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:78
#: a41a68af1b8a46389f6878c633443882
msgid "Be aware that in this state the aircraft may be very slow to respond to large control inputs and disturbances. The pilot should be extremely careful to put minimal stick inputs into the aircraft to avoid the possibility of a crash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:81
#: 891d3c59cdfc403b9726dd64f1ebd847
msgid "Test AltHold"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:83
#: 6926a8b76080439c9b515fc2d1518d18
msgid "This test will allow to test the altitude controller and ensure the stability of your aircraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:85
#: 86fe088c60ef40438c606881f9a7b5e9
msgid "Check :ref:`MOT_HOVER_LEARN <MOT_HOVER_LEARN>` is set to 2. This will allow the controller to learn by itself the correct hover value when flying."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:87
#: deb963728a59476b80c28d9c5865b78d
msgid "Take off in STABILIZE and increase altitude to 5m. Switch to AltHold and be ready to switch back to STABILIZE. If the aircraft is hovering at a very low hover throttle value you may hear a reasonably fast oscillation in the motors. Ensure the aircraft has spent at least 30 seconds in hover to let the hover throttle parameter converge to the correct value. Land and disarm the aircraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:89
#: 0771dfabe4dc4d89b74bcf8a9dea401a
msgid "Set these parameters on ground and preferably disarm (A confident pilot could set them in flight with GCS or CH6 tuning knob):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:91
#: 25b8ceb2eda1490e887794cabd56d410
msgid ":ref:`PSC_D_ACC_I<PSC_D_ACC_I>` to 0.2 x :ref:`MOT_THST_HOVER <MOT_THST_HOVER>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:92
#: 03b41eda6dd74585a03b4cc3da51d054
msgid ":ref:`PSC_D_ACC_P<PSC_D_ACC_P>` to 0.1 x :ref:`MOT_THST_HOVER <MOT_THST_HOVER>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:94
#: e64f3367f1c743d4a5880a54bfc8347e
msgid "In Copter 4.6 and earlier these parameters were named ``PSC_ACCZ_I`` and ``PSC_ACCZ_P`` and were scaled 10x larger:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:96
#: e8478ca3824442479f60c25b32105167
msgid ":ref:`PSC_D_ACC_I<PSC_D_ACC_I>` to 2 x :ref:`MOT_THST_HOVER <MOT_THST_HOVER>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:97
#: 72dc0454720c4436821282a40b52031e
msgid ":ref:`PSC_D_ACC_P<PSC_D_ACC_P>` to :ref:`MOT_THST_HOVER <MOT_THST_HOVER>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:99
#: 1fdad9b59e3a49c78d3627322be5f089
msgid "if AltHold starts to oscillate up and down the position and velocity controllers may need to be reduced by 50%. These values are: :ref:`PSC_D_POS_P<PSC_D_POS_P>` and :ref:`PSC_D_VEL_P<PSC_D_VEL_P>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:101
#: 678472e83fd2492ab4c5333cc4ef6ea4
msgid "In Copter 4.6 and earlier :ref:`PSC_D_VEL_P<PSC_D_VEL_P>` was named ``PSC_VELZ_P`` and :ref:`PSC_D_POS_P<PSC_D_POS_P>` was named ``PSC_POSZ_P``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:104
#: 1e3e3273082a4f19bb9272e472357290
msgid "Harmonic Notch Filtering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:106
#: a617d2a9db80419bb43fc22b198bbedf
msgid "After you have a hover without oscillations the next step is to get get a good notch filter setup to reduce noise to the  PID controllers. A good set of notch filtering parameters is critical to a good tune."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:111
#: 676fc11da7ba47698160ba41198776f4
msgid "To get a notch filter setup you need to hover your vehicle for at least 30 seconds with no pilot input and with :ref:`INS_LOG_BAT_MASK<INS_LOG_BAT_MASK>` set to 1. This will enable FFT logging which will guide the correct setup of the notch filters. You should then carefully read the :ref:`common-imu-notch-filtering` documentation and setup a harmonic notch to remove the noise from your gyros."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:115
#: 19810ad7ef10440ea46718e14b53387a
msgid "Eliminating noise with the notch filters will dramatically improve the quality of your tune."
msgstr ""
